# ==============================================================================
# CUSTOM OVERRIDE: Disable OpenWrt Default DUID Generation
# ==============================================================================
# OpenWrt normally uses this script on first boot to generate a random RFC 4361
# Type 4 DUID-UUID and saves it to /etc/config/network (dhcp_default_duid).
#
# We are intentionally skipping this generation for the following reasons:
#
# 1. Cloning Immunity: Saved DUIDs cause severe DHCP IP conflicts when configs
#    are cloned across multiple hardware units via 'sysupgrade' or backups.
# 2. Network Architecture: Our network architecture strictly relies on
#    standard RFC 2131 MAC-based DHCP Client IDs (Type 01).
# 3. Determinism: We dynamically generate unique, collision-proof Layer 2
#    MAC addresses per VLAN (02:00:VID:MAC_SUFFIX) via the 'vlan_mac_check'
#    init service.
#
# Exiting 0 prevents generation and allows OpenWrt to delete this script 
# normally after first boot.
# ==============================================================================

exit 0
